Optimal Solution - Prim’s algorithm using a min-heap to compute the minimum cost to connect all points via Manhattan distance.
                   Model points as a complete graph with Manhattan distances and apply Prim’s MST algorithm to greedily connect the closest unvisited point each time.

class Solution {
    public int minCostConnectPoints(int[][] points) {
        // Number of points
        int N = points.length;
        // Adjacency list: point -> list of {distance, neighborIndex}
        Map<Integer, List<int[]>> adj = new HashMap<>();
        // Build a complete graph with Manhattan distances
        for (int i = 0; i < N; i++) {
            int x1 = points[i][0];
            int y1 = points[i][1];
            for (int j = i + 1; j < N; j++) {
                int x2 = points[j][0];
                int y2 = points[j][1];
                // Manhattan distance between point i and j
                int dist = Math.abs(x1 - x2) + Math.abs(y1 - y2);
                // Add edges in both directions
                adj.computeIfAbsent(i, k -> new ArrayList<>()).add(new int[]{dist, j});
                adj.computeIfAbsent(j, k -> new ArrayList<>()).add(new int[]{dist, i});
            }
        }
        // Total cost of Minimum Spanning Tree
        int res = 0;
        // Set to track visited points in MST
        Set<Integer> visit = new HashSet<>();
        // Min-heap storing {edgeCost, pointIndex}
        PriorityQueue<int[]> minH =
                new PriorityQueue<>(Comparator.comparingInt(a -> a[0]));
        // Start Prim’s algorithm from point 0
        minH.offer(new int[]{0, 0});
        // Continue until all points are included
        while (visit.size() < N) {
            int[] curr = minH.poll();
            int cost = curr[0];
            int i = curr[1];
            // Skip if point already included in MST
            if (visit.contains(i)) {
                continue;
            }
            // Add edge cost and mark as visited
            res += cost;
            visit.add(i);
            // Add all outgoing edges from the current point
            for (int[] nei : adj.getOrDefault(i, Collections.emptyList())) {
                int neiCost = nei[0];
                int neiIndex = nei[1];
                // Push only unvisited neighbours
                if (!visit.contains(neiIndex)) {
                    minH.offer(new int[]{neiCost, neiIndex});
                }
            }
        }
        // Return total minimum cost to connect all points
        return res;
    }
}

Time Complexity :- O(N² log N).
Space Complexity :- O(N²).
